# the argument of descartes-cogito.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
logic	s5kd
atom	think	I thus think, wishing to think that all was false
atom	exist	I, who thus thought, am somewhat (I am)
atom	indubitable	the truth "I think, therefore I am" is so certain and evident that no ground of doubt the sceptics could allege, however extravagant, could shake it
atom	accept_first	I accept "I think, therefore I am" as the first principle of the philosophy I was in search of
# "absolutely necessary that I, who thus thought, should be somewhat" read as necessity of the whole conditional; it could also be read think -> []exist
P1	S1	□(think → exist)
P2	S1	think	kind empirical
P3	S1	indubitable
# "I might, without scruple, accept" read as permission (ought/permitted), not possibility
A1	-	indubitable → P accept_first	kind normative
C	S1	P accept_first	from P3 A1
